# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — build-context hygiene (PLATFORM_CONVENTIONS.md §12.7).
#
# Two reasons this file is mandatory, not cosmetic:
#  1. CORRECTNESS. `COPY cpp cpp` from a tree where the README quick start was
#     followed carries cpp/build/CMakeCache.txt, whose CMAKE_HOME_DIRECTORY
#     points at the HOST path; `cmake -S . -B build` inside the image then
#     aborts with "source directory ... does not match the source used to
#     generate cache". Likewise rust/target and java/out poison incremental
#     state with host paths.
#  2. SIZE. Without this file the context is ~950 MB (rust/target 668 MB,
#     data/ 259 MB, java/out, .git) for images that need a few MB of source.
#
# Everything a build stage needs must be COPYed explicitly; anything listed
# here can never be. tests/harness/check_deployment.py asserts that every
# `COPY <src>` in every Dockerfile exists AND is not excluded here.
# =============================================================================

# --- build trees (host-absolute paths baked into caches)
cpp/build/
rust/target/
java/out/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
python/build/
python/dist/
*.egg-info/

# --- generated data (regenerated inside the pipeline image; never baked in)
data/raw/
data/normalized/
data/features/
data/orderbooks/
# data/reference/ IS required by the C++/Rust golden tests — do NOT exclude it.

# --- VCS, editor, OS
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
*.log

# --- research artefacts and pickles (not needed by any image)
research/models/*/model.pkl
*.parquet
